{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794851756,"nonce":"LR460f3O8VeSG+xIWLeedZDeI/w=","title":"ash_host_watch runs its handler on the program's thread, so an await on what it settles hangs","message":"Reported by hxn (hxn-bd session, 2026-11-16), not reproduced here. An HDLL watches a wake word with\n`ash_host_watch`; the handler runs on the program's own thread. When the program `await`s a future that\nthe browser agent settles through that handler, `await` blocks the thread the handler needs, and the\nprogram hangs. hxn-gpu-webgpu and hxn-gpu-webgl2 stopped using it: they settle answers on a thread of\ntheir own, watching the wake word with `memory.atomic.wait32`, and still start their agent with\n`ash_host_agent`.\n\nTo do: say in docs/wasm/host-abi.md which thread the handler runs on and what a blocked program does to\nit (`ash_host_watch` is not described there at all), and decide whether the handler should run on an\nagent of its own.","files":null}]}